**Verdicts:** YES = no denials and nothing unconfined · NO = fix the root causes below first ·
REVIEW = no denials, but the listed services have no policy (enforcing will not confine them) ·
NOT ASSESSABLE = SELinux disabled, nothing is evaluated, so "0 denials" proves nothing.

**Limits of this report:** denials suppressed by `dontaudit` rules are not logged and therefore
not counted (temporarily `semodule -DB` while reproducing, then `semodule -B`). Code paths that
did not run during the window (month-end jobs, DR) are not represented.

